      "writtenOn": "2023-12-18T18:26:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "One concern regarding this is that a non-null `*DeapexerInfo` and a non-null error can be returned at the same time. In such case, how can we ensure that the caller properly raises an error? WDYT about returning a non-null `*DeapexerInfo` iff error is null (and `di` is non null), and return null `*DeapexerInfo` when multiple of them is found in order to prevent the users wrongly consuming it and enforce to raise an error?",
