      "writtenOn": "2023-12-18T23:30:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You are correct, we do not do any dexing during ninja execution when building with prebuilts.\n\nHowever, we do use `compile_dex` and `shared_library` during [Soong analysis](https://cs.android.com/android/_/android/platform/build/soong/+/8070c4b457d890455bd7c8437ab84d02d9e7f3bc:java/sdk_library.go;l\u003d1141-1146;drc\u003d8ff105860d20f2ccbb8d8044bf562f94100b7f6a;bpv\u003d1;bpt\u003d0) to determine whether a prebuilt apex contains a dex jar. In the example you provided, `framework-adservices` uses `shared_library`. I have updated this test to use `shared_library` as well\n\n(In the long run, neither of this properties of java_sdk_library_import should matter. Whether a prebuilt apex contains dex code or not should be defined by the `prebuilt_apex` and not by `java_sdk_library_import`)",
      "parentUuid": "5356c56c_1f8f1744",
